# Code Quality Guardrails

Apply these defaults across languages unless the user requests otherwise:

- Keep changes minimal and idiomatic for the surrounding codebase.
- Avoid comments that restate obvious code; comment intent and trade-offs only.
- Avoid speculative defensive branches unless required by known boundaries.
- Do not use type-escape shortcuts to bypass real type/contract issues.
- Prefer fixing root causes over adding wrappers, indirection, or noise.

Rule id: cq-1
